※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4514

※ Lifting something takes it out of the program and hands it to the compiler,
※ which has no representation to give back: a type is not a value here and
※ neither is a name.  The places a lift may stand are the ones where the
※ compiler answers rather than the program computes -- inside `⎕typeof`, on
※ either side of a comparison the compiler settles, and after `⌈` or `⌊`, where
※ what it answers is the largest or smallest value the lifted type has.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = ⌜u8⌝
    0u6
